@startuml CatInk_Casos_Uso_General
title Diagrama de Casos de Uso - CatInk (vision general del alcance)

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #EF3363
  ArrowColor #475569
}

actor "Visitante"          as VIS
actor "Lector\nregistrado" as LEC
actor "Aspirante\na vacante" as ASP
actor "Redactor"           as RED
actor "Editor"             as EDI
actor "Super Admin"        as ADM

actor "SMTP Hostinger"     as SMTP <<system>>
actor "YouTube Data API"   as YT   <<system>>
actor "Geolocalizacion IP" as GEO  <<system>>
actor "Cron del hosting"   as CRON <<system>>

VIS <|-- LEC
RED <|-- EDI
EDI <|-- ADM

rectangle "Sistema CatInk" {
  usecase "Consultar contenido publico"       as G1
  usecase "Gestionar cuenta de lector"        as G2
  usecase "Participar\n(comentarios y likes)" as G3
  usecase "Leer sin conexion (PWA)"           as G4
  usecase "Redactar y publicar contenido"     as G5
  usecase "Curar portada y CMS"               as G6
  usecase "Gestionar publicidad"              as G7
  usecase "Gestionar mailing\ny suscriptores" as G8
  usecase "Gestionar bolsa de trabajo"        as G9
  usecase "Moderar comunidad"                 as G10
  usecase "Administrar usuarios\ny permisos"  as G11
  usecase "Consultar metricas\ny bitacora"    as G12
}

VIS --> G1
VIS --> G2
VIS --> G4
LEC --> G3
ASP --> G9
RED --> G5
RED --> G12
EDI --> G6
EDI --> G7
EDI --> G8
EDI --> G9
EDI --> G10
ADM --> G11

G2 --> SMTP
G8 --> SMTP
G9 --> SMTP
G6 --> YT
G1 --> GEO
G7 --> GEO
G8 <-- CRON
G5 <-- CRON

note bottom
  Detalle por subsistema en:
    09-casos-uso-publico.puml (Visitante, Lector, Aspirante)
    10-casos-uso-admin.puml   (Redactor, Editor, Super Admin)

  Redactor, Editor y Super Admin no son roles fijos en la BD:
  se derivan de los 14 campos perm_* de la tabla usuarios.
  Cada campo es una mascara de bits: 1 = crear, 2 = leer,
  4 = editar, 8 = eliminar (15 = las cuatro acciones),
  evaluada por mapearPermisos() en views/helpers/helper.php.
end note

@enduml
